From ce00d1bf1c0f15f6af381d064ad3307495583083 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Axis Dev <axis-dev@example.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 11:17:43 +0000
Subject: feat: add Axis pricing page with live Paddle pricing
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds a public /pricing page for Axis — required by Paddle as part of
account verification, alongside the refund policy added previously.

Also required: since this marketing site is Regent's agency-pitch site
(bespoke systems engineering, no self-serve SaaS anywhere else on it),
Axis pricing didn't have a natural home here yet. This adds it as its own
top-level page rather than folding it into an existing section.

- src/lib/paddle-pricing.ts: server-side helper that calls Paddle's
  Pricing Preview API (POST /pricing-preview) directly via fetch for all
  6 Axis prices (Starter/Pro/Advanced x monthly/annual). Response shape
  verified against a live call to the API. Results are localized by the
  visitor's IP (via x-forwarded-for) when available, so UK/Ireland/
  Australia visitors see the GBP/EUR/AUD overrides configured in Paddle
  automatically, with a 1-hour fetch cache since prices don't need to be
  real-time-fresh.
- src/app/(public)/pricing/page.tsx: the page itself. Server component,
  three plan cards driven entirely by the Paddle response — no
  hand-typed prices to drift out of sync. Fails soft (shows plan/feature
  info without prices, plus a small notice) if the Paddle call errors,
  rather than 500ing the page.
- src/components/Navbar.tsx, Footer.tsx: added Pricing links
- src/app/sitemap.ts: registered /pricing

Requires a new PADDLE_API_KEY env var in this repo's deployment config
(not previously used here) — same server-side API key already added to
axis-business-hub's .env.example for the webhook route; this can reuse
the same value. This repo has no .env.example file to extend, so this
is called out here instead.

Also uses a placeholder signup link (https://app.axis.example.com/signup)
on each plan's CTA button — swap for the real Axis app URL before merging.

Verified: tsc --noEmit and next build both pass clean. Build produces
/pricing as a dynamic (server-rendered) route rather than static, since
it reads request headers for IP-based localization — this is expected
and intentional, not a regression.
